    "2:1–2 — 'Now when Jesus was born in Bethlehem of Judaea in the days of Herod the king, behold, there came wise men from the east to Jerusalem, saying, Where is he that is born King of the Jews?' Matthew skips the shepherds and the manger-detail Luke loves. He starts the public story with Gentiles reading a star and a paranoid client-king. 'King of the Jews' is their phrase. It will be heard again on the titulus above the cross (27:37). The Gospel is already stretching a wire from this house to that hill.",
