      "title": "The Kingdom Sentence Both Men Preach",
      "icon": "📯",
      "body": "John: 'Repent ye: for the kingdom of heaven is at hand' (3:2). Jesus: the same words (4:17). Matthew wants you to hear the continuity before you hear the difference. John can only point. Jesus can bring the kingdom because he is the King the genealogy already named. Repentance in both mouths is not a mood. It is a turn of the whole life toward a reign that has come close enough to touch."
