    "Exodus 17:1–7 and Numbers 14 — Massah and the larger wilderness unbelief. 'If thou be the Son' is that old demand in a new mouth.",
    "Hosea 11:1 with Matthew 2:15 — the Son called out of Egypt now walks the wilderness. Chapters 2–4 are one Israel-recap, not three isolated stories.",
    "Isaiah 9:1–7 — Galilee of the Gentiles sees a great light, and a child is given whose government sits on David's throne. Matthew 4:14–16 quotes the light and leaves the child-king standing just offscreen.",
    "Matthew 16:21 — the second 'from that time.' 4:17 begins the public preaching; 16:21 begins the road to the cross. Matthew built two hinges on purpose."
