  "doctrinal": "Teacher-only: I read the Sermon as instruction for disciples now, not as a constitution filed away until a future millennial administration. 28:20 ('teaching them to observe all things whatsoever I have commanded you') will not let me park chapters 5–7 in a postponed age. I also refuse the opposite dodge — treating the mountain as a pure mirror to show you cannot do it and then never climbing it. Jesus means the heart-deepening of the law, and he means it for the people who will follow him. On 5:17 I sit with 'fulfil = bring to intended goal,' not 'fulfil = abolish by completing a checklist.' On 5:32 I would name the exception as Matthew's real text and not pretend Mark's silence erases it; I read porneia as sexual unfaithfulness that breaks the one-flesh union, and I would say that as mine without running a church-court in the lesson. Leave 5:38–42 aimed at personal revenge and occupation-pressure. Do not let a student use 'turn the other cheek' as a slogan that decides every magistrate question the rest of Scripture still has to answer (Romans 13:1–4).",
