    "scene": "A hillside above the lake. Fishermen who left nets yesterday are sitting closest. Behind them, the crowd that has already seen the healings of 4:23–25. Jesus sits. That is the signal class has begun.\n\nHe does not start with a rule. He starts by congratulating the people nobody congratulates — the poor in spirit, the mourners, the meek, the hungry for a righteousness they do not yet have. Then he puts his own 'I say unto you' beside words they have heard since childhood, and the mountain becomes a courtroom where motive is on the stand.",
