    "6:1 — The thesis of the first half of the chapter: 'Take heed that ye do not your alms before men, to be seen of them: otherwise ye have no reward of your Father which is in heaven.' The Greek behind 'alms' here is dikaiosunē again — righteousness, the same word as 5:6, 10, 20. Some manuscripts read 'alms'; the older flow is 'righteousness.' Either way, 6:2–18 is 5:20 worked out in three practices every synagogue already honored: giving, prayer, fasting. The danger is not the practice. It is the audience. If men are the audience, men are the whole paycheck.",
