    "6:16–18 — Fasting. Disfigured faces, the look of hunger worn as clothing. Anoint the head, wash the face, fast for the Father. Isaiah 58:3–7 had already attacked a fast that oppressed workers and then waited for God to notice. Jesus is in that stream. He assumes his disciples will fast ('when ye fast'), which will matter when 9:14–15 explains why they are not fasting yet while the bridegroom is with them.",
