  "doctrinal": "Teacher-only: I read John's question as faith under pressure, not as unbelief to be shamed. I read 11:27 as one of the highest Christology lines in the book — mutual exclusive knowledge of Father and Son — and I would say that out loud rather than tiptoe. On 11:12 I will not pretend the Greek is tidy; I sit nearest 'the kingdom is under assault and people are also pressing toward it,' and I will not spend the hour there. The load-bearing invitation is 11:28–30: rest is in a yoke, and the yoke is a person.",
